\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S4}{\ignorespaces Summary of different GLMMs predicting speciation probability. Different models are shown across the y-axis, labeled by the simulation model parameter included as a covariate along with the hump-shaped relationship effect of abundance. Estimated effect sizes and 95\% confidence intervals are shown in the left hand panel. The quadratic term for abundance from each model is shown in the middle panel. The right hand panel shows the shift in abundance value at which probability of speciation reaches its peak. This shift is shown relative to the model without simulaton model parameters as covariates. The magnitudes each arrow represent how the location of peak speciation probability would shift with an increase in the simulation model covariate.}}{16}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
